    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nSupporting *all* possible cases is [explicitly not the goal](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b2ac6522f7a54b475d9fad711b938eefc6d3d0a6/doc/mini-icons.txt#L30-L33) of 'mini.icons'. The approximate line of what to support is along the lines of \"Add new support only for more or less established filetypes\" (as in `:h 'filetype'`). This allows keeping 'mini.icons' relatively lean while delegating to `vim.filetype.match` to determine how to match file name to a filetype.\n\nAs far as I can tell, `jspf` is not an established filetype as it is only a fragment of a JSP file (which *has* `jsp` filetype). At least, Neovim codebase doesn't have a single mention of the former filetype.\n\nSo I think the best approach here is for the user to have `vim.filetype.add({ extension = { jspf = 'jsp' } })` somewhere in their config. This will both recognize `jspf` extension when opening it *and* automatically make 'mini.icons' work.\n\nTo make it usable for other users, it might be better to make a PR to Neovim/Vim that adds support for `jspf` extension.",
